-- title:
--   Integrality of q-expansions on both charts after base change
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of the extension $L \subseteq L((q))$ which is assumed to equal [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the elements of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by all quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of one and the same weight $k$ for $\Gamma$ viewed inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$, with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,p_g \neq 0$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as its fraction field, acting on $K$ compatibly with its action on $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero and have $q$-expansion the coefficientwise image in $L((q))$ of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), namely $q^{-1}$ times the image in $\mathbb{Q}[[q]]$ of the integral power series `jNum`. The conclusion is a conjunction: every element $b$ of `chartAlgFin A K j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and likewise every element $b$ of `chartAlgInf A K j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, is the coefficientwise image under $A \to L$ of some Laurent series $y \in A((q))$.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion principle in the form needed for the two-chart model of the modular curve attached to $\Gamma$: the chart rings over a discrete valuation ring $A$, obtained as the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$ in the base-changed $q$-expansion function field $K = L \cdot \mathbb{Q}(X(\Gamma))$, consist of series with all coefficients in $A$. It is used in the analysis of $X_1(Mp)$ over rings such as $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[\zeta_p]$, in particular for the Gauss presentations of the chart algebras and for the reduction of Laurent places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_coeffMap_eq_coe_of_mem_chartAlg_twoChartModel_laurentBaseChange.lean

import Mathlib
